  "scope": "Native resident boot config, terminal reset/power, managed update paths, journalv2-v5/claim bytes, slot ordering, replay, checked atomic ownership/cleanup, durable claim store and pre-runtime recovery. Existing native runtimeboot/driverpolicy/system-transition owners retain order and real shutdown receipts. R4SYS/boot call typed owners directly. Original external119consumers, SDK/Contract and independent Zig Recovery stay unchanged; no userland policy moves into Kernel.",
  "ownership_safety": [
    "Explicit private C records and enum tags; all journal/payload/component offsets pinned on both sides. Actual active capacities preserve sentinel boundaries; fixed spans/optional/union projections carry no compiler-specific layout.",
    "Three181728-byte journalrecords and192KB/64KB/4KBbuffers stayresident, journal initialized inplace. No large metadata temporary or borrowed mutable state across VFS/persist/callback; exact file identities/fingerprints and caller FSgate remain authoritative.",
    "Global claim/generation/name buffers and atomic checksum scratch receive independent existing native wait-spanning SyncUnwindGuard admission across different drive requests; exact owner/generation release, reentrant scratch reuse refused. No new FSrequest and no RuntimeOwner held across I/O. Static missing-serialization finding, not a claimed data-corruption reproduction.",
    "Journalv2-v5 compatibility, v5canonical bytes/FNV/strict fields/slot ambiguity/forwardbatch/rollback/lastgood/full-package and per-tuplecleanup retained. No stage deletion on cleanup; previous backups need exact fingerprints.",
    "Recovery precedes loader/config/fonts/R4D caches, kernel/preload restoration still needs actual Limine followstart. Bootspace/partition/backup/archive rules unchanged. Reset computes clock parameters before firstwrite, rawTSC grace onlyafterwrite, original bounded8042/S5 fallbacks; ordinarypoweroff is not DriverShutdown."
  ],
